# STORY: ammo research, card markings and the M.A.R.S. supply line (claude/AMMO_SUPPLY_v1.md).
# Text only; BUILD wires the ids (claude/BRIEF_FOR_BUILD_AmmoSupply.txt). Generated by story_tools/gen_ammo_text.py.
# Loads after gijoe_story_act1.rul on purpose: its STR_CRATE_SERIAL_PLATE_UFOPEDIA replaces batch 1's.
extraStrings:
- type: en-US
  strings: &id001
    STR_SUPPLIER_NAME: Larkhall Ordnance Supply
    STR_CRATE_SERIAL_PLATE_UFOPEDIA: 'Roadblock read me the plate off a crate in the barn. The serial belongs to no army and no maker on any register we can reach. It carries a lot number, C-0417, that
      nobody admits to.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}Someone stamps their own lot numbers. That''s a factory, somewhere.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}- Scarlett{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}ROADBLOCK: Every round in our own stores has a lot
      stamp on it too. Never looked at ours twice. Might be worth reading the cards on what we''ve got.'
    STR_CARD_MARKINGS_GJ_AMMO_A556: Lot C-0421, stamped on the base.
    STR_CARD_MARKINGS_GJ_AMMO_A556_30: Lot C-0422, stamped on the base.
    STR_CARD_MARKINGS_GJ_AMMO_A9MM: Lot C-0419, stamped on the base.
    STR_CARD_MARKINGS_GJ_AMMO_A45: Lot C-0408, stamped on the base.
    STR_CARD_MARKINGS_GJ_AMMO_A44: Lot C-0405, stamped on the base.
    STR_CARD_MARKINGS_GJ_AMMO_A12G: Lot C-0411, stamped on the base.
    STR_CARD_MARKINGS_GJ_AMMO_A762BELT: Lot C-0430, stamped on the base.
    STR_CARD_MARKINGS_GJ_AMMO_A50: Lot C-0433, stamped on the base.
    STR_CARD_MARKINGS_GJ_AMMO_A83: Lot C-0440, stamped on the base.
    STR_CARD_MARKINGS_GJ_AMMO_A81: Lot C-0441, stamped on the base.
    STR_CARD_MARKINGS_GJ_AMMO_ABOLT: Lot C-0402, stamped on the base.
    STR_CARD_MARKINGS_GJ_AMMO_AFLARE: Lot C-0401, stamped on the base.
    STR_CARD_MARKINGS_GJ_AMMO_AJAV: Lot C-0450, stamped on the base.
    STR_CARD_MARKINGS_GJ_AMMO_ALASER: Lot C-0460, stamped on the base.
    STR_CARD_MARKINGS_HC_AP_AMMO: Lot C-0435, stamped on the base.
    STR_CARD_MARKINGS_AC_AP_AMMO: Lot C-0434, stamped on the base.
    STR_CARD_MARKINGS_SMALL_ROCKET: Lot C-0442, stamped on the base.
    STR_CARD_MARKINGS_PISTOL_CLIP: Lot C-0419, stamped on the base.
    STR_CARD_MARKINGS_RIFLE_CLIP: Lot C-0420, stamped on the base.
    STR_CARD_MARKINGS_ALIEN_GRENADE: Lot C-0417, stamped on the base.
    STR_CARD_MARKINGS_GJ_AMMO_A762AK: Lot C-0425, stamped on the base.
    STR_CARD_MARKINGS_PLASMA_PISTOL_CLIP: 'No lot stamp. A part number, etched: MRS-11.'
    STR_CARD_MARKINGS_PLASMA_RIFLE_CLIP: 'No lot stamp. A part number, etched: MRS-11.'
    STR_CARD_MARKINGS_HEAVY_PLASMA_CLIP: 'No lot stamp. A part number, etched: MRS-11.'
    STR_AMMO_PISTOL_CLIP: 9 mm Pistol Round (Cobra)
    STR_AMMO_PISTOL_CLIP_UFOPEDIA: 'ROADBLOCK: Standard 9 millimetre, full metal jacket, a 30-round box for the Uzi. Nothing clever about it. Cobra''s men carry it because it''s cheap, it''s everywhere,
      and it kills you just as dead.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}We''ve checked it in our guns. It feeds clean, so whatever we take off them, we use. Knowing what they shoot also tells us what our vests have to stop:
      the next armour job in the lab starts ahead.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}SCARLETT: The lot stamp is C-0419. The boxes come from Firth Precision, Rotterdam. Firth has an address, a telex number and a registered
      agent in Glasgow. It does not have a factory.'
    STR_AMMO_RIFLE_CLIP: 5.56 mm Rifle Round (Cobra)
    STR_AMMO_RIFLE_CLIP_UFOPEDIA: 'ROADBLOCK: 5.56 NATO, 30 to the magazine. The same round we fire. Cobra''s riflemen got it the same way we did, by buying it, which tells you how big their wallet is.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}It
      fits our rifles, so captured stock goes straight into our stores. And we know now exactly what our armour has to stop.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}SCARLETT: Lot C-0420. Maker of record: Calder Arms Export, Antwerp.
      Calder''s warehouse is a rented room over a bakery. Same registered agent in Glasgow as Firth. Somebody owns a lot of companies that don''t make anything.'
    STR_AMMO_ALIEN_GRENADE: Cobra Fragmentation Grenade
    STR_AMMO_ALIEN_GRENADE_UFOPEDIA: 'ROADBLOCK: A fragmentation grenade with a short fuse, and the casing scored so it breaks even. Better than ours, if I''m honest. Somebody designs these for a living.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}We
      can throw what we capture. Knowing the pattern helps the lab with what our vests have to stop.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}SCARLETT: Lot C-0417. The same number as the plate on the ranch crates. The fuse body
      says Arbroath Industrial, Lisbon. Arbroath, Calder and Firth all file their accounts through the same Glasgow office.'
    STR_AMMO_GJ_AMMO_A762AK: 7.62 mm AK Round (Cobra)
    STR_AMMO_GJ_AMMO_A762AK_UFOPEDIA: 'ROADBLOCK: The short 7.62, thirty to a curved magazine. Cobra hands it out with the AKs it buys by the crate. Heavy, hits hard, carries well.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}Captured
      magazines fit the captured rifles, so they''re ours to use.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}SCARLETT: Lot C-0425. Calder Arms Export again. Their invoices are in sterling, not dollars or guilders. The money ends
      up in Scotland.'
    STR_AMMO_PLASMA_PISTOL_CLIP: Pulse Pistol Cell
    STR_AMMO_PLASMA_PISTOL_CLIP_UFOPEDIA: 'ROADBLOCK: This isn''t a cartridge. It''s a sealed cell, and when it''s spent it''s warm and empty. I don''t know who makes these. Nobody sells them.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}We
      can study how it''s built, and that tells the lab what our armour has to take.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}SCARLETT: No lot stamp. A part number etched in the casing: MRS-11. Whoever made the lot-stamped rounds
      didn''t make this, or doesn''t want to be seen to.'
    STR_AMMO_PLASMA_RIFLE_CLIP: Pulse Rifle Cell
    STR_AMMO_PLASMA_RIFLE_CLIP_UFOPEDIA: 'ROADBLOCK: A bigger cell for the pulse rifle. Same build, more of it.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}Knowing its output helps the lab with our armour.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}SCARLETT:
      Part number MRS-14. The same etching as the pistol cell.'
    STR_AMMO_HEAVY_PLASMA_CLIP: Heavy Pulse Cell
    STR_AMMO_HEAVY_PLASMA_CLIP_UFOPEDIA: 'ROADBLOCK: The heavy pulse gun''s cell. If one of these cracks, stand somewhere else.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}Knowing its output helps the lab with our armour.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}SCARLETT:
      Part number MRS-19.'
    STR_AMMO_QUALITY_AUDIT: Ammunition Quality Audit
    STR_AMMO_QUALITY_AUDIT_UFOPEDIA: 'ROADBLOCK: We pulled a sample of every lot in our stores and test-fired it. A few bad boxes went back. What''s left is checked, and it groups tighter.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}SCARLETT:
      Every box we own came from Larkhall Ordnance Supply. Their lot numbers start C-04. So do Cobra''s.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}I''m not saying what that means yet.'
    STR_CLEAN_SUPPLY: Clean Supply
    STR_CLEAN_SUPPLY_UFOPEDIA: 'SCARLETT: Larkhall Ordnance Supply, Firth Precision, Calder Arms Export, Arbroath Industrial. Four names, one office in Glasgow, one owner behind it, and the same mark we
      found on the weapon from the Drome: M.A.R.S.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}We have been buying our ammunition from the people who arm Cobra. Every box we paid for, they got paid for.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}HAWK: That
      stops today. General Flagg will take over every purchase this team makes, personally, through the Pentagon. It will cost more and it will be slower. It will be clean.'
    STR_EVENT_FLAGG_HIT: GENERAL FLAGG IS DOWN
    STR_EVENT_FLAGG_HIT_DESCRIPTION: 'HAWK: General Flagg was shot leaving the Pentagon twenty minutes ago. His car is pinned on a side street and the shooters are still there.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}He was on
      his way to sign the new supply contract. Somebody didn''t want it signed. Get a team to Washington, now.'
    STR_FLAGG_RESCUE: 'Washington: Flagg Ambushed'
    STR_BRIEFING_FLAGG_RESCUE_TITLE: 'OPERATION: SHIELD'
    STR_BRIEFING_FLAGG_RESCUE: 'HAWK: Flagg is down behind his car, hit and bleeding. His driver is dead. Cobra has the street.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}Reach him, keep him alive, and get him to the extraction
      point. Don''t try to take him through the shooters. He can''t run.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}If we fail, they''ll take him with them. Don''t fail.'
    STR_EVENT_FLAGG_RETIRES: THE GENERAL STEPS DOWN
    STR_EVENT_FLAGG_RETIRES_DESCRIPTION: 'HAWK: The doctors say General Flagg will walk again. They also say he won''t be going back into the field.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}He''s been asked to serve as Secretary
      of Defense, and he''s said yes. His first order was to put every purchase this team makes through his own office. Our supply is clean.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}I''ve worked for worse men. I don''t think I''ll
      work for a better one.'
    STR_EVENT_LIBERTY_RENAMED: U.S.S. FLAGG
    STR_EVENT_LIBERTY_RENAMED_DESCRIPTION: 'The Navy has renamed the carrier U.S.S. Liberty in honour of General Flagg. She sails as the U.S.S. Flagg.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}KEEL-HAUL: Same ship, same crew, a
      better name. All hands, battle stations.'
    STR_CARRIER_NAME_LIBERTY: U.S.S. Liberty
    STR_CARRIER_NAME_FLAGG: U.S.S. Flagg
    STR_ART_KEEL_HAUL_TEXT_RENAMED: 'KEEL-HAUL{NEWLINE}G.I. Joe - Rear Admiral (O-8){NEWLINE}Real name: Everett P. Colby{NEWLINE}Specialty: Carrier commander; Pilot{NEWLINE}Birthplace: Charlottesville,
      Virginia{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}DOSSIER{NEWLINE}Keel-Haul commands the U.S.S. Flagg, the aircraft carrier that serves as the team''s floating base, renamed for the general who gave the team its supply back.
      A Virginia naval officer of the old school, he runs his ship with discipline and his crew with pride. When his guns speak, the battle changes.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}IN THE FIELD{NEWLINE}Signature weapon:
      Sidearm{NEWLINE}Signature move: Fleet Support: naval gunfire on a target area if the U.S.S. Flagg or a TTBP is in range; otherwise a coastal battery strike{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}"All hands, battle stations."'
- type: en-GB
  strings: *id001
